    "stem": "The phrase \"flagged up\" (Para. 2) is the closest in meaning to _______.",
    "stemTranslation": null,
    "options": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "found.",
        "isCorrect": false,
        "distractorType": "CONCEPT_DISTORTION",
        "analysis": "词义偏差。flag up 强调在初筛时打上专门标记以便后续跟进复审，并非单纯的“被发现（found）”。"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "revised.",
        "isCorrect": false,
        "distractorType": "CONCEPT_DISTORTION",
        "analysis": "时序与语义颠倒。flagged up 只是把可疑论文标示出来送审，尚未进入修改（revised）阶段。"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "marked.",
        "isCorrect": true,
        "analysis": "词义推断题。定位至第二段第三句：“Manuscripts will be flagged up for additional scrutiny by the journal's internal editors, or by its existing Board of Reviewing Editors or by outside peer reviewers.” 句中 flag 作动词，本义为插旗标示，短语 flag up 意为“做出标记、凸显标明”。论文稿件将被内部编辑或审稿人‘标记出来（flagged up）’以接受额外细审，故 marked（被标记的）与 flagged up 词义最为切合一致。",
        "vocab": [
          {
            "word": "revised",
            "ipa": "",
            "meaning": "修改，修订",
            "level": "red",
            "isSelfAnnotated": true
          }
        ],
        "selfAnnotated": true
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "stored.",
        "isCorrect": false,
        "distractorType": "CONCEPT_DISTORTION",
        "analysis": "概念偏差。语境强调挑选送审，与论文手稿“被封存/被储存（stored）”毫无关联。"
      }
    ],
    "officialAnswer": "C",
    "standardType": "VOCAB",
    "type": null,
    "targetSentences": null,
    "verbatimEvidence": null,
    "synonymMapping": {
      "marked": "flagged up (打上旗标/标记提醒注意 -> 被标记)"
    },
    "methodologyReview": "词汇推断题。利用语境逻辑与词根隐喻：flag 原意为旗帜，在此作动词引申为‘插旗打标签、标记警示’，其后搭配 for additional scrutiny（以便接受额外严密审查），逻辑上即等价于被编辑 marked（标出/标记）。",
